  "problems": "",
  "rationale": "Setting --aligner hisat2 replaces STAR index generation and alignment. The test profile supplies hisat2.tar.gz, so the index is untarred, HISAT2_BUILD (which needs 200 GB) does not run, and the splice sites are extracted from the GTF. Because hisat2 has neither an RSEM nor a Salmon quantification branch, the BAM-based Salmon quantification and its DESeq2 QC are dropped. Every BAM-derived step (markduplicates, QC, bigWig, StringTie) and MultiQC reruns on the new HISAT2 BAMs; the --additional_fasta with --hisat2_index combination only triggers a warning."
